The eigenvectors $vb(u_1), ..., vb(u_n)$ can be chosen orthonormal, $vb(u_i)^dagger vb(u_j) = delta_(i j)$. Equivalently the matrix $matbold(P)$ of eigenvectors can be chosen unitary, $matbold(P)^dagger = matbold(P)^(-1)$, so

$ matbold(P^dagger) matbold(A) matbold(P) = matbold(D). $

For a real symmetric matrix the eigenvectors can be taken in $RR^n$ with $vb(u_i)^TT vb(u_j) = delta_(i j)$, equivalently $matbold(P)$ orthogonal with $matbold(P)^TT = matbold(P)^(-1)$ and $matbold(P)^TT matbold(A) matbold(P) = matbold(D)$.
